WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.280
Place a workload by evaluating its data, latency, capability, scale, and dependencies.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.585
Sensitive documents may need to remain on approved local systems.

00:00:08.585 --> 00:00:11.480
An interactive assistant may require low latency near the user.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.915
A large batch job may tolerate network delay and benefit from temporary cloud GPUs.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:20.280
A long-context request may need a hosted model if local memory cannot support it,

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.400
but only when the input is permitted to leave.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.280
Coding assistance illustrates the trade.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.010
Public code or generic questions may use either environment,

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.990
while proprietary repositories may require local processing or an approved private

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:31.885
endpoint.

00:00:31.885 --> 00:00:35.635
Document review can separate local extraction and redaction from external generation.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:39.620
Vision workloads may stay at the edge when images are sensitive or bandwidth is limited,

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.840
while large offline image batches move to controlled cloud capacity.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.380
Retrieval-augmented generation has several placement points: source documents, chunking,

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.400
embeddings, vector search, prompt assembly, and generation.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.440
Each can create copies or metadata.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.330
Agent workflows add tools, credentials, memory, and side effects,

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.720
so placement must consider what the agent can access,

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.680
not only where the language model runs.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.483
Use a decision record for each workload.

00:01:01.483 --> 00:01:06.455
State allowed data classes, required model capabilities, latency and availability targets,

00:01:06.455 --> 00:01:10.640
expected volume, cost limit, logging policy, and approved fallback.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.300
Revisit placement when requirements or providers change.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.775
The correct answer can differ between tasks inside one application;

00:01:16.775 --> 00:01:18.800
that is the purpose of intentional hybrid design.
